  note    17.0.0, `unicode`'s own; Go's x/net names its own in `idna.UnicodeVersion` (15.0.0 in v0.49.0)

capability idna/nameprep  IDNA 2003: RFC 3490's ToASCII and ToUnicode with RFC 3491's nameprep profile of RFC 3454's stringprep
  heroes  refused: IDNA 2003 is obsolete since IDNA 2008 (RFC 5890 to 5894, 2010); its mapping, which turned "ß" into "ss" and could not write some names at all, is what UTS #46's transitional flag keeps, and UTS #46 marks it deprecated
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  encodings.idna.nameprep, stringprep.in_table_a1, stringprep.in_table_b1, stringprep.map_table_b2, stringprep.map_table_b3, stringprep.in_table_c11, stringprep.in_table_c12, stringprep.in_table_c11_c12, stringprep.in_table_c21, stringprep.in_table_c22, stringprep.in_table_c21_c22, stringprep.in_table_c3, stringprep.in_table_c4, stringprep.in_table_c5, stringprep.in_table_c6, stringprep.in_table_c7, stringprep.in_table_c8, stringprep.in_table_c9, stringprep.in_table_d1, stringprep.in_table_d2

